30,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Oh man, the yards are a mess! Our devices are ancient, and trying to switch systems during peak season is a disaster. We need something that can handle our actual reality.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings are concerning. The board ignores operating costs, and separate licenses for software tend to climb every year. We need a price that stays stable over time.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It's just as I feared. Last winter, nobody took ownership of the outage, and our warehouse rules change so often that a frozen project scope is useless.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that our old tools just stop getting updated because testing takes too long, and the external data move in 2018 left a huge mess!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Servas,,"We are losing our institutional memory. Key administrators are retiring, and the depot supervisors often ignore standard training to stick to their own old routines.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if the rules change that fast, won't a rigid system just break? We need something flexible that doesn't crash the depot floor.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, if external teams leave a mess, we should be very careful about who handles the migration. It could cost us more in the long run.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, exactly. A fixed configuration is a trap. And @Servas, if the supervisors ignore training, a complex system will simply be abandoned.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, that's true! If we just buy a fancy system but the data is wrong, it's like having a shiny car with no engine!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, you hit the mark. We need a solution that doesn't rely on a few exhausted people or a training manual that the crews will simply discard.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I just want to make sure we don't have another paper-dispatch nightmare. Whatever we pick has to be rugged and simple enough for the yard.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm leaning toward a bundled agreement. My data shows that separate add-ons are where the budget leaks. We need a predictable, all-in cost.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We need a single point of accountability. I cannot accept another situation where four different vendors point fingers at each other while the system is down.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Rin,,And it has to be something we can actually keep updated! I don't want a system that just ages in place because it's too scary to touch.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must prioritize the human transition. If the vendor doesn't provide deep, ongoing support, our remaining staff will simply break under the pressure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
