55,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Looking at these, Anchor seems great because they stay through the rollout. But Meridian's fixed process might be too rigid for our yards.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Tessera's subscription is a risk if the marketplace adds costs, but Corvus's modular licenses are exactly what I saw climbing in the invoices.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Meridian's regional team provides a single point of contact, but their fixed configuration is a nightmare for our changing warehouse rules. Anchor is better.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Tessera uses a partner for migration, which sounds like the 2018 mess. Anchor's engineering team being present sounds much safer for the data!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Servas,,Anchor's presence through rollout is the only way to ensure the depot supervisors actually adopt the system. Tessera's partner firm feels too distant.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I agree! Having the engineers there means they can see the old yard devices and actually fix things instead of just guessing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, if Anchor is on-site, maybe the costs are more transparent? I'm worried about the ""hidden"" fees of a cloud marketplace like Tessera.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, Anchor is on our own servers, which means we control the environment. No more finger-pointing between four different cloud providers.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, exactly! And since it's built for transport operators, it won't be a ""general"" tool that we have to surround with spreadsheets.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Servas,,It is the most compassionate choice for our staff. Anchor provides the hand-holding our retiring administrators and stubborn supervisors desperately need.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm sold on Anchor. It's the only one that feels like it understands the grit of the depot floor.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. An outright purchase or a stable on-site cost is better than the creeping fees of modular or marketplace systems.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Anchor solves the accountability problem and the deployment risk. It is the most logical choice to avoid our past failures.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Rin,,I love it! It's a specialized tool that comes with the people to make it work. I'm voting for Anchor!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Servas,,We have found a path that honors both the technical needs and the human spirit. I am in full agreement.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
